# __PROJECT__

A PostgreSQL extension with a managed background worker compiled with .NET Native AOT.
Requires .NET 10, a native C toolchain and PostgreSQL 18 with server headers.

Restore the matching local tool and register PostgreSQL, then run the managed
and native tests:

```console
dotnet tool restore
dotnet ankus init --pg18 /path/to/pg_config
dotnet test
```

The backend fixture publishes the library and starts an isolated cluster with
shared preload enabled. Its worker test verifies that another PostgreSQL process
executes a transaction and publishes the result through shared memory.
Build and server logs remain under `src/__PROJECT__/bin/ankus-test-logs/`.

Publish and install the extension:

```console
dotnet ankus publish
dotnet ankus install
```

Add the library to `postgresql.conf`, preserving any other preloaded libraries,
then restart PostgreSQL:

```ini
shared_preload_libraries = '__EXTENSION__'
```

Install the SQL declarations and inspect the worker:

```sql
CREATE EXTENSION __EXTENSION_IDENTIFIER__;
SELECT worker_process(), worker_result();
```

The worker connects to `postgres` using the bootstrap superuser, executes
`SELECT 42` in its own transaction and waits ten seconds between observations.
Adapt the database, role and query in `src/__PROJECT__/Workers.cs` for your use
case. Configuration reload wakes the worker; server shutdown terminates it.
An unsuccessful worker exit restarts after five seconds.

Ordinary SQL functions remain in `Functions.cs`. Package versions live in
`global.json` and `Directory.Packages.props`. The local tool version is pinned in
`.config/dotnet-tools.json`.

SQL regression files live beside the extension project under `pg_regress/`.
The generated `sql/setup.sql` and `expected/setup.out` create the extension.
Worker regression tests also require the library's shared preload setting.
